  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64022,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Uterus and rarely in sites of ectopic pregnancy {2240354; 9675597; 12405916}</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:50:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64023,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Placental site nodule/plaque (PSN) and atypical placental site nodule (APSN) are generally incidental findings in women of childbearing age and may present with vaginal bleeding {2240354}. There is usually no association with elevated hCG levels.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:50:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64024,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The true incidence is unknown {25675185}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:50:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64025,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:50:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64026,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PSN arises from trophoblast with differentiation towards chorionic-type intermediate trophoblast. APSN is a recently proposed trophoblastic lesion that is considered a precursor to epithelioid trophoblastic tumour {25675185}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:50:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64027,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesions are nodular and 4&ndash;10&nbsp;mm in size.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:50:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64028,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>PSNs are nodules or plaques, usually &lt;&nbsp;5&nbsp;mm in size, with chorionic-type intermediate trophoblast arranged in single cells or cords and embedded in an abundant hyalinized matrix. Typical features include focal cytological atypia, enlarged hyperchromatic nuclei with smudgy chromatin, and absent or low mitotic activity. The Ki-67 proliferation index is &lt;&nbsp;5% {2240354}.</p>\r\n<p>APSN shows features intermediate between those of typical PSN and epithelioid trophoblastic tumour. Larger nodule size (5&ndash;10&nbsp;mm), increased cellularity, marked nuclear atypia, increased mitotic activity, and a Ki-67 proliferation index of &gt;&nbsp;5% are proposed criteria for diagnosis {2240354; 25675185; 30407075}. However, definitive diagnostic criteria have not yet been established.</p>\r\n<p>Lesional cells show reactivity for cytokeratins, &alpha;-inhibin, GATA3, PLAP, and p63, whereas hPL and MCAM (CD146) are often negative. The Ki-67 proliferation index is &lt;&nbsp;5% for PSN and 5&ndash;10% for APSN. Cyclin&nbsp;E positivity has been described in some APSNs as in epithelioid trophoblastic tumour; PSN lacks cyclin&nbsp;E expression {16931955}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-30T17:02:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64029,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lesional cells may lead to abnormal cervical cytology.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:50:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64030,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:50:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64031,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> typical morphological features.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> Ki-67, PLAP, p63, and inhibin immunohistochemistry.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:50:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64032,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:50:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64033,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PSN is a benign lesion. Patients with APSN should undergo imaging studies to rule out an underlying mass lesion that requires clinical follow-up {25675185; 23688193; 18983471}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:50:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]